(The encoding mechanics, one focused check each.

 Every instruction is encoded at 0x401000, with the label distant at 0x500000
 and the label behind at 0x400800, and its bytes are compared with the bytes
 nasm -f bin gives the same line placed the same way. Each check also
 measures the instruction with its labels somewhere else, which must give
 the same size, since pass one measures before any label is placed. Then a
 few instructions vas must refuse, with the message it gives.

 Run it from anywhere; it reads no files. It prints a count for each
 mechanic and exits 1 if any check fails.)

see "./records.vox".
see "../../../../tools/vas/encoder.vox".

a list called 'encoding table' is [].
a list called 'row mnemonics' is [].
a text called 'table problems' is 'prepare the encoder' with 'encoding table' and 'row mnemonics'.
If 'table problems' is not "" then,
  Print "The encoding table has problems:\n{table problems}",
  Exit 1.

a map called registers is 'the register map'.
a buffer called scratch.
a list called 'mechanics in order' is [].
a map called tally is {}.
a number called 'checks run' is 0.
a number called 'checks passed' is 0.

(Count a check under its mechanic, keeping the mechanics in the order they
 first appear.)
To 'count the check' with a text called mechanic and a boolean called 'it passed'.
  a boolean called 'it was seen' is tally's "seen {mechanic}".
  If 'it was seen' is false then, append mechanic to 'mechanics in order', Set tally's "seen {mechanic}" to true.
  a number called run is tally's "run {mechanic}".
  Set tally's "run {mechanic}" to run add 1.
  increment 'checks run'.
  If 'it passed' then,
    a number called passed is tally's "passed {mechanic}",
    Set tally's "passed {mechanic}" to passed add 1,
    increment 'checks passed'.

To 'check the encoding' with a text called mechanic and a text called line and a text called expected.
  a map called 'placed labels' is {"distant": 0x500000, "behind": 0x400800}.
  a map called record is 'the record of the line' with line and 'placed labels' and registers.
  a text called problem is record's "problem".
  a buffer called output.
  If problem is "" then, set problem to 'encode the instruction' with record and 0x401000 and 'encoding table' and 'row mnemonics' and output.
  a text called encoded is 'the bytes in hex' of output.
  a map called 'moved labels' is {"distant": 16, "behind": 0x7FFF0000}.
  a map called 'moved record' is 'the record of the line' with line and 'moved labels' and registers.
  a number called size is 'the size of the instruction' with 'moved record' and 'encoding table' and 'row mnemonics' and scratch.
  a boolean called 'it passed' is false.
  If problem is "" and encoded is expected and size is output's size then, set 'it passed' to true.
  If 'it passed' is false then, Print "FAIL ({mechanic}) {line}: nasm gives {expected}; vas gives {encoded}, measures {size} bytes; {problem}".
  'count the check' with mechanic and 'it passed'.

To 'check the refusal' with a text called line and a text called expected.
  a map called 'placed labels' is {"distant": 0x500000, "behind": 0x400800, "unreachable": 0x90000000}.
  a map called record is 'the record of the line' with line and 'placed labels' and registers.
  a buffer called output.
  a text called problem is 'encode the instruction' with record and 0x401000 and 'encoding table' and 'row mnemonics' and output.
  a boolean called 'it passed' is false.
  If problem is expected and output's size is 0 then, set 'it passed' to true.
  If 'it passed' is false then, Print "FAIL (refusals) {line}: expected the refusal \"{expected}\"; vas says \"{problem}\" and lays down {output's size} bytes".
  'count the check' with "refusals" and 'it passed'.

(The REX prefix: W for a 64-bit operation; R, X and B for a register 8 to 15
 in the reg field, the index and the base; none for a 32-bit operation on
 the first eight registers; and a REX of its own for spl, bpl, sil and dil.)
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "mov eax, ebx" and "89 d8".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "mov rax, rbx" and "48 89 d8".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "mov rax, r9" and "4c 89 c8".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "mov r9, rax" and "49 89 c1".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "mov rax, [rbx + r9*2]" and "4a 8b 04 4b".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "mov r15, [r13 + r14*8 + 16]" and "4f 8b 7c f5 10".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "mov sil, al" and "40 88 c6".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "cmp dil, 1" and "40 80 ff 01".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "movzx eax, bpl" and "40 0f b6 c5".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "sete sil" and "40 0f 94 c6".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "mov [rbp-104], r11b" and "44 88 5d 98".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "mov spl, 5" and "40 b4 05".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "pop r12" and "41 5c".
'check the encoding' with "REX prefix" and "push r15" and "41 57".

(The ModRM byte: a register, memory with no displacement, a byte of
 displacement and four, and a digit in the reg field.)
'check the encoding' with "ModRM byte" and "add rax, rbx" and "48 01 d8".
'check the encoding' with "ModRM byte" and "mov rax, [rbx]" and "48 8b 03".
'check the encoding' with "ModRM byte" and "mov rax, [rbx + 8]" and "48 8b 43 08".
'check the encoding' with "ModRM byte" and "mov rax, [rbx + 1024]" and "48 8b 83 00 04 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "ModRM byte" and "neg qword [rbx]" and "48 f7 1b".
'check the encoding' with "ModRM byte" and "dec rdi" and "48 ff cf".

(The SIB byte: a base of rsp or r12, which the r/m field cannot name, and an
 index with each scale, with and without a base.)
'check the encoding' with "SIB byte" and "mov rax, [rsp]" and "48 8b 04 24".
'check the encoding' with "SIB byte" and "mov rax, [rsp + 8]" and "48 8b 44 24 08".
'check the encoding' with "SIB byte" and "mov rax, [r12]" and "49 8b 04 24".
'check the encoding' with "SIB byte" and "mov rax, [r12 + 300]" and "49 8b 84 24 2c 01 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "SIB byte" and "mov rax, [rbx + rcx]" and "48 8b 04 0b".
'check the encoding' with "SIB byte" and "mov rax, [rbx + rcx*2]" and "48 8b 04 4b".
'check the encoding' with "SIB byte" and "mov rax, [rbx + rcx*4 + 8]" and "48 8b 44 8b 08".
'check the encoding' with "SIB byte" and "mov rax, [rbx + rcx*8 + 1000]" and "48 8b 84 cb e8 03 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "SIB byte" and "lea rax, [rcx*4 + 16]" and "48 8d 04 8d 10 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "SIB byte" and "mov rax, [rdx + r12*4]" and "4a 8b 04 a2".

(A base of rbp or r13 with no displacement: the r/m bits mean something
 else without one, so a byte of 0 goes in. r13 as an index needs none.)
'check the encoding' with "rbp and r13 bases" and "mov rax, [rbp]" and "48 8b 45 00".
'check the encoding' with "rbp and r13 bases" and "mov rax, [r13]" and "49 8b 45 00".
'check the encoding' with "rbp and r13 bases" and "mov rax, [r13 + rcx]" and "49 8b 44 0d 00".
'check the encoding' with "rbp and r13 bases" and "mov rax, [rax + r13]" and "4a 8b 04 28".
'check the encoding' with "rbp and r13 bases" and "mov rax, [rbp + rcx*2]" and "48 8b 44 4d 00".
'check the encoding' with "rbp and r13 bases" and "lea rsi, [rbp]" and "48 8d 75 00".

(A displacement takes one byte from -128 to 127, and four past either end.)
'check the encoding' with "disp8 and disp32" and "mov rax, [rbx + 127]" and "48 8b 43 7f".
'check the encoding' with "disp8 and disp32" and "mov rax, [rbx + 128]" and "48 8b 83 80 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "disp8 and disp32" and "mov rax, [rbx - 128]" and "48 8b 43 80".
'check the encoding' with "disp8 and disp32" and "mov rax, [rbx - 129]" and "48 8b 83 7f ff ff ff".
'check the encoding' with "disp8 and disp32" and "inc qword [rbp-144]" and "48 ff 85 70 ff ff ff".

(An immediate takes the sign-extended byte form when the processor gets the
 number back from one byte, measured against the width of the operation, and
 the long form otherwise; the accumulator has short long forms of its own.)
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "add rax, 127" and "48 83 c0 7f".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "add rax, 128" and "48 05 80 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "add rbx, 128" and "48 81 c3 80 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "add rbx, -128" and "48 83 c3 80".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "add rbx, -129" and "48 81 c3 7f ff ff ff".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "and bx, 0xFFFF" and "66 83 e3 ff".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "and bx, 0xFCFF" and "66 81 e3 ff fc".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "and ax, 0x1234" and "66 25 34 12".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "cmp r11d, 0xFFFFFFFF" and "41 83 fb ff".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "cmp eax, 1000" and "3d e8 03 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "cmp al, 0xFF" and "3c ff".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "add dl, 200" and "80 c2 c8".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "push 10" and "6a 0a".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "push 1000" and "68 e8 03 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "imul rax, rax, 10" and "48 6b c0 0a".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "imul rcx, 200" and "48 69 c9 c8 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "test rax, 1" and "48 a9 01 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "test r15, 1" and "49 f7 c7 01 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "imm8 and imm32" and "mov qword [rax + 8], -1" and "48 c7 40 08 ff ff ff ff".

(A mov into a 64-bit register takes nasm's shortest form: a 32-bit mov,
 which zero-extends, for 0 to 0xFFFFFFFF; the sign-extended 32-bit form for
 a small negative number; and the whole 64 bits otherwise, and always for a
 label.)
'check the encoding' with "mov of an immediate" and "mov rax, 0" and "b8 00 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "mov of an immediate" and "mov r13, 0xFFFFFFFF" and "41 bd ff ff ff ff".
'check the encoding' with "mov of an immediate" and "mov rax, -1" and "48 c7 c0 ff ff ff ff".
'check the encoding' with "mov of an immediate" and "mov rax, -2147483648" and "48 c7 c0 00 00 00 80".
'check the encoding' with "mov of an immediate" and "mov rax, -2147483649" and "48 b8 ff ff ff 7f ff ff ff ff".
'check the encoding' with "mov of an immediate" and "mov rax, 0x100000000" and "48 b8 00 00 00 00 01 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "mov of an immediate" and "mov r13, distant" and "49 bd 00 00 50 00 00 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "mov of an immediate" and "mov edx, 0xFFFFFFFF" and "ba ff ff ff ff".
'check the encoding' with "mov of an immediate" and "mov r8b, ' '" and "41 b0 20".

(A jump or a call is measured from the address of the next instruction, and
 is always 32 bits, forwards or back.)
'check the encoding' with "rel32" and "call distant" and "e8 fb ef 0f 00".
'check the encoding' with "rel32" and "jmp behind" and "e9 fb f7 ff ff".
'check the encoding' with "rel32" and "jne distant" and "0f 85 fa ef 0f 00".
'check the encoding' with "rel32" and "jz behind" and "0f 84 fa f7 ff ff".

(The operand-size prefix for 16 bits, F2 and F3 for SSE and rep, each
 before the REX prefix.)
'check the encoding' with "legacy prefixes" and "mov [rsp + 12], bx" and "66 89 5c 24 0c".
'check the encoding' with "legacy prefixes" and "mov bx, [rsp + 8]" and "66 8b 5c 24 08".
'check the encoding' with "legacy prefixes" and "addsd xmm0, xmm1" and "f2 0f 58 c1".
'check the encoding' with "legacy prefixes" and "movq xmm0, [r14]" and "f3 41 0f 7e 06".
'check the encoding' with "legacy prefixes" and "cvtsi2sd xmm1, r12" and "f2 49 0f 2a cc".
'check the encoding' with "legacy prefixes" and "cvttsd2si r12, xmm0" and "f2 4c 0f 2c e0".
'check the encoding' with "legacy prefixes" and "movsd xmm8, [rbp-8]" and "f2 44 0f 10 45 f8".
'check the encoding' with "legacy prefixes" and "rep movsb" and "f3 a4".
'check the encoding' with "legacy prefixes" and "roundsd xmm0, xmm0, 0" and "66 0f 3a 0b c0 00".

(The two-byte opcodes behind 0F.)
'check the encoding' with "the 0F escape" and "syscall" and "0f 05".
'check the encoding' with "the 0F escape" and "movzx rcx, dl" and "48 0f b6 ca".
'check the encoding' with "the 0F escape" and "imul rax, rbx" and "48 0f af c3".
'check the encoding' with "the 0F escape" and "btr rax, 63" and "48 0f ba f0 3f".
'check the encoding' with "the 0F escape" and "cmovge r12, rbx" and "4c 0f 4d e3".

(The x87 instructions, D8 to DF with a digit in the reg field.)
'check the encoding' with "x87" and "fild qword [rsp]" and "df 2c 24".
'check the encoding' with "x87" and "fldcw [rsp + 12]" and "d9 6c 24 0c".
'check the encoding' with "x87" and "fnstcw [rsp + 8]" and "d9 7c 24 08".
'check the encoding' with "x87" and "fstp qword [rsp]" and "dd 1c 24".
'check the encoding' with "x87" and "fmul qword [rsi + rcx*8]" and "dc 0c ce".
'check the encoding' with "x87" and "fdiv qword [rsi + 22*8]" and "dc b6 b0 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "x87" and "fstp qword [r12 + 8]" and "41 dd 5c 24 08".

(Memory relative to the instruction pointer: 32 bits from the end of the
 whole instruction, immediate and all, forwards or back; and an absolute
 address, written without rel.)
'check the encoding' with "rel addressing" and "lea rsi, [rel distant]" and "48 8d 35 f9 ef 0f 00".
'check the encoding' with "rel addressing" and "lea rdi, [rel distant + 20]" and "48 8d 3d 0d f0 0f 00".
'check the encoding' with "rel addressing" and "cmp qword [rel distant], 0" and "48 83 3d f8 ef 0f 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "rel addressing" and "mov qword [rel distant], 0" and "48 c7 05 f5 ef 0f 00 00 00 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "rel addressing" and "mov byte [rel distant + 40], '0'" and "c6 05 21 f0 0f 00 30".
'check the encoding' with "rel addressing" and "lea rax, [rel behind]" and "48 8d 05 f9 f7 ff ff".
'check the encoding' with "rel addressing" and "movsd xmm1, [rel distant]" and "f2 0f 10 0d f8 ef 0f 00".
'check the encoding' with "rel addressing" and "mov rax, [distant]" and "48 8b 04 25 00 00 50 00".

(The short forms nasm prefers: a shift by one, a shift by cl, the
 accumulator forms, and xchg with rax.)
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "shl rax, 1" and "48 d1 e0".
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "shr rax, cl" and "48 d3 e8".
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "shl rax, 52" and "48 c1 e0 34".
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "xchg rax, rbx" and "48 93".
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "xchg rbx, rax" and "48 93".
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "xchg rsi, rdx" and "48 87 f2".
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "or al, 0x20" and "0c 20".
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "and eax, 0o7777" and "25 ff 0f 00 00".
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "cmp rax, -4096" and "48 3d 00 f0 ff ff".
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "xor ebx, ebx" and "31 db".
'check the encoding' with "short forms" and "inc al" and "fe c0".

(What vas refuses: a mnemonic outside the table, operands no row fits,
 memory whose size nothing gives, rsp as an index, and a target out of
 reach of 32 bits.)
'check the refusal' with "pushf" and "vas has no encoding for the instruction pushf".
'check the refusal' with "mov [rax], 5" and "vas has no encoding for these operands: mov [rax], 5".
'check the refusal' with "inc [rax]" and "vas has no encoding for these operands: inc [rax]".
'check the refusal' with "movzx eax, [rbx]" and "vas has no encoding for these operands: movzx eax, [rbx]".
'check the refusal' with "add r9d, 1000" and "vas has no encoding for these operands: add r9d, 1000".
'check the refusal' with "mov rax, [rbx + rsp*2]" and "rsp cannot be the index register of a memory operand".
'check the refusal' with "jmp unreachable" and "the target is too far from the instruction to reach in 32 bits".
'check the refusal' with "lea rax, [rel unreachable]" and "the target is too far from the instruction to reach in 32 bits".

For each mechanic in 'mechanics in order',
  a number called run is tally's "run {mechanic}",
  a number called passed is tally's "passed {mechanic}",
  Print "{passed} of {run}: {mechanic}".
Print "{checks passed} of {checks run} encoder mechanics checks pass.".
If 'checks passed' is not 'checks run' then, Exit 1.
